 "_ergonomics": "Face buttons drawn at their real Dreamcast diamond positions (Y top, X left, B right, A bottom, the same shape Xbox later copied), but Flycast's own libretro mapping swaps A/B and X/Y onto the RetroPad slots: its A slot reads as the Dreamcast's B, its B slot reads as the Dreamcast's A, and the same swap applies to X/Y. Confirmed against shell/libretro/libretro.cpp's own input descriptor table, not assumed. The `input` values below are already corrected for that swap; do not 'fix' them to match the label without re-checking the source. No Select: the real pad has none. L/R are single analog triggers (RetroPad L2/R2, not L1/R1, since Flycast reads them there), no stacked pair like PS1's. D-pad above, stick below, stacked on the left the way real Dreamcast emulators (RDC/Revive) draw it, both L/R and Start/Menu pulled up near the very top of the strip to match. Second pass after the first one shipped a d-pad too small to read as a cross: TouchControlPad.drawDpad's fixed 6pt corner radius on each arm dominates and breaks the plus shape once the frame drops much below ~100pt square, not an aspect-ratio problem as first suspected.",
